  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting partnerships for a transition to a circular economy in Cuba</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project represents the continuation of FIPEE project implemented by UNIDO ITPO Italy (between April 2019 and December 2023). It is built on lessons learned in the previous phase and it is focused on promote and strengthen sustainable, green, and inclusive economic development in Cuba.  The project aims to create a regional center for the circular economy (CCE) for the municipalities of the Province of Sancti Spiritus. The center will have a central headquarter and some municipal level centers, connected in a hub &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; spoke system with each other and with the rest of the Country. So that each territorial node (Municipality) is a gateway for businesses, researchers and citizens. Each center will be equipped with offices, laboratories, research infrastructures and facilities with trained staff, connected to future industrial pilot plants for waste recycling and recovery or for the production of renewable energy (designed in this project and implemented with future external resources to be found).  The project seeks to achieve the following outputs:  Establish a Regional Center for the Circular Economy and provide it with appropriate equipment and capacities to deliver technical assistance and promote circular economy practices among SMEs.  Create a system of sustainable economic development through the int</narrative>
  </description>
